      "content": "\n```vue src/components/Modal.vue\n<script setup>\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div class=\"fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center\">\n    <!-- Backdrop -->\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 bg-black/50 backdrop-blur-sm\" @click=\"close && $emit('close')\"></div>\n\n    <!-- Modal Box -->\n    <div\n      v-bind=\"$attrs\"\n      class=\"relative z-10 bg-base-100 rounded-2xl shadow-2xl border border-base-300 w-full max-w-lg max-h-[90vh] flex flex-col mx-4 animate-fade-in\"\n    >\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center justify-between px-6 py-4 border-b border-base-300\">\n        <slot name=\"title\">\n          <span class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-base-content\"></span>\n        </slot>\n        <button\n          v-if=\"close\"\n          class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm btn-circle text-base-content/60 hover:text-error transition-colors\"\n          @click=\"$emit('close')\"\n        >\n          <i class=\"fa-solid fa-xmark text-lg\"></i>\n        </button>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Body -->\n      <div class=\"flex-1 overflow-y-auto px-6 py-4\">\n        <slot></slot>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Footer -->\n      <div v-if=\"$slots.footer\" class=\"px-6 py-4 border-t border-base-300 flex justify-end gap-2\">\n        <slot name=\"footer\"></slot>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>\n\n<script>\nexport default {\n  inheritAttrs: false,\n  props: ['close', 'scope'],\n  mounted() {\n    // Attach to the provided scope element, or fall back to the root App element\n    const target = this.scope || this.$root.$el\n    target.appendChild(this.$el)\n  },\n  beforeUnmount() {\n    // Clean up when modal is destroyed\n    if (this.$el.parentNode) {\n      this.$el.parentNode.removeChild(this.$el)\n    }\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n### Changes made:\n\n- \u2795 **`scope` prop added** \u2014 accepts a DOM element to use as the mount target\n- \ud83c\udfaf **Smart mounting** \u2014 `mounted()` now uses `this.scope` if provided, otherwise falls back to `this.$root.$el` (App root)\n- \ud83e\uddf9 **`beforeUnmount` cleanup** \u2014 safely removes the modal from the DOM when the component is destroyed, preventing memory leaks\n\n### Usage example:\n\n```vue\n<!-- Attach to App root (default behavior) -->\n<Modal :close=\"true\" @close=\"show = false\">...</Modal>\n\n<!-- Attach to a specific element -->\n<Modal :close=\"true\" :scope=\"$refs.myContainer\" @close=\"show = false\">...</Modal>\n```",
